1
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:06,381
(Penny:)So, Bernadette, how goes the hunt
for bridesmaid dresses?

2
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:09,758
(Bernadette:)Well, if you don't mind looking
like an orange traffic cone, great.

3
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:13,759
GirIfriends, I have the answer
to our dress problems.

4
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,640
(Bernadette:)Really?
Twelve years ago...

5
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:17,937
(Amy:)...my cousin Irene
and her entire family died...

6
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:21,771
...in a horrific carbon-monoxide accident
the night before her wedding.

7
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:26,153
- That's horrible.
- Yes and no.

8
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:29,233
(Amy:)All those bridesmaids dresses
remain unused...

9
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:31,614
(Amy:)...and available to us for free.

10
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:35,289
(Amy:)So it seems that cloud
of odorless, deadly gas...

11
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,162
(Amy:)...had a silver lining after all.

12
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:41,494
(Amy:)Check it out, still in the bags.
The gowns, not the bridesmaids.

13
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:47,092
(Bernadette:)I don't know. Dead people's dresses?

14
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:50,635
Yeah, and cap sleeves? Ehh...

15
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,471
Hmm. I was hoping
you wouldn't notice.

16
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,636
Irene was a slave to a good bargain
when it came to clothes...

17
00:00:56,806 --> 00:01:00,186
(Amy:)...and, sadly, as it turned out,
space heaters.

18
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,023
(Sheldon:)Ladies, please.

